From fef1a058e9b25fc2fd17ca706531c0bdd8162b95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 17:19:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] desktop: per-plugin JSON pools; single-flight
 hub-sync /status

>From 05:00 to 08:05 PST on 2026-11-13 the runners plugin kept 11 slow (~30 s)
/v1/fleet reads in flight per 15 s poll. Overlapping polls and their retries
filled the shared 50-socket JSON keep-alive pool, and every other request
(kanban/board 1964, hub-sync/status 501) queued past its 30 s total deadline:
2803 timeouts in 30 min. hermes-mods 61a0321c fixed runners, but nothing
stopped the next plugin from doing the same.

Plugin pools (electron/api-transport.ts, json-fetch.ts): every
/api/plugins/<id>/... JSON request now uses an agent for that plugin, created
lazily and capped at PLUGIN_POOL_MAX_SOCKETS = 8. A Node agent caps sockets per
origin, and each connection is its own origin, so the cap applies per
(connection, plugin). A plugin that floods queues only behind itself. Core
routes keep the shared 50-socket JSON pool, kanban and hub-sync keep their own
sockets, and the probe pool is unchanged. One shared /api/plugins/* pool was
rejected: kanban/board is itself a plugin route and would still starve.

Single-flight audit:
- kanban/board, kanban/boards: already single-flight. A React Query interval
  tick or a new observer joins the read in flight (no cancelRefetch), and
  socket frames wait for it (invalidateAfterInFlight). The shared board poll
  options are now boardPoll()/boardPollMs(), pinned by
  api.board-poll.test.ts: a read slower than four poll intervals, page and
  count pill both polling, a live frame mid-read, at most one read in flight.
- hub-sync/status: was not single-flight. learnHubGatewayName runs for every
  answering gateway on every board poll, with no in-flight dedupe and no
  caching of a miss. Now one /status read is in flight per connection, and a
  miss is not asked again for 60 s.

Tests:
- json-fetch.test.ts: 60 concurrent runners reads held for 30 s, then a
  kanban/board read with a 3 s deadline. Fails on main ("Timed out connecting
  to Hermes backend after 3000ms"). Passes with the fix, and the flood holds
  exactly PLUGIN_POOL_MAX_SOCKETS sockets.
- hub-sync.test.ts: 3 overlapping askers make 3 /status calls on main and 1
  with the fix; a miss is not asked again within 60 s.
